   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the issuance of specialty plates for members of AMVETS",
    "basePrintNo": "S3936",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3936-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §404-y, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3936\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to the issuance of specialty plates for members of AMVETS\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis legislation would allow American Veterans (AMVETS) to obtain a\nspecialty license plate that bears special wording that recognizes\nboth the membership and organization of the applicant. This\ndistinctive plate would be issued upon proof that is satisfactory to\nthe Commissioner of the Department of Motor Vehicles.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: 1. The vehicle and traffic law is amended by adding a new\nsection 404-x establishing distinctive plates for AMVETS. Any member\nof the AMVETS, residing in the state, shall be issued a license plate\nbearing the term \"American Veteran\", \"AMVET\" or \"AMVETS\". 2. Requires\nthat satisfactory proof of membership be presented. 3. Establishes\nthat this distinguished plate will be issued in the same manner as\nother numbered license plates upon the payment of the regular\nregistration fee and a one-time service charge of ten dollars. 4.\nBeing part of \"AMVETS\" will mean that the federally chartered\ncorporation is advocating on behalf of all American Veterans.\n\nSection 2: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nAt this time, The State of New York makes available many different\ndistinctive license plates to members of various groups. The AMVETS is\na service organization that supports and assists the honorable men and\nwomen, who are currently serving or have served, in the U.S.  Armed\nForces from World War II until now, including the National Guard and\nReserves. These members of AMVETS have served our country well and\ncontinue to be leaders in.our communities. Therefore, this legislation\nwould make it possible for the honorable members of this organization\nto display their association with a specific New York State license\nplate.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2015-16: A9031 - referred to transportation\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
